; Entity handler: Satan's fireball (room 24); its body flies the arrows too
;
; The fireballs Satan fires in room 24 (templates #R$BCE2, #R$BCF2 and #R$BD02, spawned in a volley of three by
; #R$BB57). This 3-instruction entry removes the fireball as soon as Satan has been turned into smoke (#R$8522 nonzero,
; see #R$BC69): #R$B08E clears the handler word and goes on to the next slot. Otherwise it falls through to #R$B6ED,
; which is the handler of the arrows (#R$BC92, #R$BCA2 and #R$BCB2 are spawned with that address) and of the fireballs
; alike.
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word was popped by the RET that entered the routine)
@label=UpdateFireball
c$B6E6 LD A,($8522)  ; SatanSmoked
 $B6E9 OR A          ;
 $B6EA JP NZ,$B08E   ; Satan is gone: remove the fireball
; Entity handler: projectile flying in a straight line (arrows, fireballs), entered with SP at slot+2. Slot from a
; template (#R$BC92 on): +2 word x speed and +4 word y speed (signed 8.8, 2-pixel units per frame), +6 word x and +8
; word y (8.8, high bytes in 2-pixel units), +$A word hit box offset (y, x), +$C word hit box size (y, x), +$E word
; width and height of the sprite (draw command units), +$10 pointer to the sprite description (attribute, column in
; the sprite sheet, base page: see #R$B730). The speeds are added to the position every frame and the projectile is
; removed (slot freed by #R$B08E) when it leaves the room (y at or below PROJECTILE_Y_MAX, or x not in 0-$7F, which
; takes the negative values as well) or when the flags of the two cells at its top-left corner (the cell at (x/4, y/4)
; and the one to the right) have a tile class other than 0 (solid or harmful; ORed and masked with TILE_CLASS_MASK).
; Otherwise the position becomes the position of the draw command (y, x/4) and the hit box is tested against the monk
; (#R$A851), which continues at #R$B730 with A' = x. Cells are looked up as in the other entities: the row address
; table #R$6100 (H = $61, L = 2 * (y / 4)) gives the address of the row of the tile flag map and x / 4 is the column.
@label=UpdateArrow
*$B6ED POP HL        ; x speed
 $B6EE POP DE        ; y speed
 $B6EF POP BC        ; x
 $B6F0 ADD HL,BC     ; x moves
 $B6F1 EX DE,HL      ; DE = new x, HL = y speed
 $B6F2 POP BC        ; y
 $B6F3 ADD HL,BC     ; y moves
 $B6F4 PUSH HL       ; store y
 $B6F5 PUSH DE       ; store x
 $B6F6 LD A,H        ; y in 2-pixel units
@isub=CP PROJECTILE_Y_MAX
 $B6F7 CP $60        ; below the room (or negative)
 $B6F9 JR NC,$B716   ;
 $B6FB BIT 7,D       ; x outside 0-$7F
 $B6FD JR NZ,$B716   ;
 $B6FF SRA H         ; y / 2
 $B701 RES 0,H       ; 2 * (y / 4): index of the row in the table of words
 $B703 LD L,H        ;
 $B704 LD H,$61      ; row address table #R$6100
 $B706 LD A,D        ; x
 $B707 RRA           ;
 $B708 RRA           ;
 $B709 AND $1F       ; x / 4: cell column
 $B70B ADD A,(HL)    ; address of the cell in the tile flag map
 $B70C INC L         ;
 $B70D LD H,(HL)     ;
 $B70E LD L,A        ;
 $B70F LD A,(HL)     ; flags of the cell
 $B710 INC L         ;
 $B711 OR (HL)       ; and of the cell to its right
@isub=AND TILE_CLASS_MASK
 $B712 AND $07       ; tile class
 $B714 JR Z,$B71B    ; free: draw it
; Remove a projectile: also used by the seeds (#R$B74B). The two pushes put SP back at slot+2 (they overwrite the
; position, which does not matter) and #R$B08E then zeroes the handler word and goes on to the next slot.
@label=Projectile_Remove
*$B716 PUSH HL       ;
 $B717 PUSH HL       ;
 $B718 JP $B08E      ; free the slot
; Draw a projectile that stays: also used by the seeds (#R$B74B). SP is at slot+6, the position words (x, then y)
; are the next ones. Makes HL = x (H) and y (L), keeps x in A' for the shift phase of the sprite, makes the draw command
; position (y, x/4) and tests the hit box (#R$A851, which continues at #R$B730).
@label=Projectile_Draw
*$B71B POP HL        ; x word
 $B71C LD D,H        ; D = x
 $B71D POP HL        ; y word
 $B71E LD E,H        ; E = y
 $B71F LD L,H        ;
 $B720 LD H,D        ; HL = x (H) and y (L)
 $B721 LD A,H        ;
 $B722 EX AF,AF'     ; A' = x: its low 2 bits select the shifted copy
 $B723 SRA H         ; x / 4 = byte column
 $B725 SRA H         ;
 $B727 LD ($ACD3),HL ; position of the draw command: y, byte column
 $B72A LD HL,$B730   ; continue after the hit test
 $B72D JP $A851      ; hit test: sets the hit flag when the monk touches the box
